**TITLE: Associate, Asset Management**
**Job Summary**

* Execute asset management strategies to ensure sound management and risk mitigation across the global commercial real estate debt portfolio;
* Oversee the performance of all commercial real estate debt assets including assisting with monitoring loan performance, covenant compliance, capex tracking, IPD waterfall analysis, redemptions, prepayments, disposals, asset-level business plans, lease-up progress, borrower financials, quarterly loan reviews and on-going portfolio management workstreams;
* Produce portfolio-wide analytics to support strategic decision-making and identify emerging trends
* Operate with clear, consistent communication and expectation setting across a wide range of internal and external stakeholders, including Borrowers, Sponsors, syndicate/participant Lenders, Servicers, and other counterparties;
* Coordinating with lenders, borrowers and their respective lawyers in respect to loan redemptions, restructuring, amendments, waivers and other ad hoc requests.
* Provide competent analysis of a portfolio of loans and underlying security on a quarterly basis; including re-underwriting every quarter for internal presentation;
* Respond to requests for portfolio level due diligence and performance updates in a timely manner;
* Work with the Client AM global team to ensure accuracy and compliance with industry standards and maintain a deep understanding of loan documents, including covenants, terms, and legal requirements;
* Ensure all documentation is up-to-date and supports effective asset management and risk mitigation.
* Problem solving when issues arise at the loan or portfolio level and proactively identify and report credit risk, market risk, and operational risk within the portfolio, develop and implement risk mitigation strategies with AM team;
* Assist in preparing and present portfolio updates, performance reports, and recommendations to internal stakeholders;
* Participate in onboarding and integration of new technology solutions to enhance portfolio monitoring and analytics;
* Establish best practices, processes, and policies for loan monitoring and reporting.

**Qualifications**
**What you should have:**

* 3-5 years of experience in asset management, investment management, or financial services;
* Experience working with global or large domestic corporations, and experience in a diverse team, with responsibilities including execution of functions and tasks, improving workflows to enhance collaboration, productivity, and professional growth;
* Advanced degree in finance, business, economics, or related field;
* Strong skills in Excel and familiarity with other Microsoft Office tools;
* Exceptional communication abilities, capable of simplifying concepts;
* Proven track record of excellence in processes and workstreams in a scalable, KPI-based environment;
* Strong capabilities in both internal and external relationship management;
* Independent and collaborative working style.

**Role Description**
Reconciliation Junior Analyst


This role is to hire a Business Process Operations Junior Analyst .


**Overview Of Role/Principle Responsibilities**

* Working within the Reconciliations team in ensuring the integrity of custody and cash position data is maintained within our internal systems through our daily reconciliation processes.
* Ensure the complete reconciliation, investigation and allocation of all breaks are completed within set SLA’s and deadlines.
* The role holder will thrive in a fast-paced environment with an emphasis on meeting tight deadlines.
* A strong interest in learning and harnessing technology will help you with your role in the organisation. Key Responsibilities:
* Accountable for allocated portfolios, proactive investigation and timely follow up of queries arising from internal stakeholders, clients, counterparties, custodians and administrators;
* Perform custody transaction and position reconciliation against internal records;
* Maintain ownership of daily cash and stock breaks by conducting investigation on differences, and monitoring through timely resolution with processing teams and custodians/administrators;
* Perform outstanding OTC bilateral collateral and outstanding position reconciliation, outstanding fixed deposit positions, between internal and counterparty records and monitor through breaks resolution in a timely manner;
* Validate and update internal records with relevant transactions, such as fees and income;
* Work through high volumes, prioritise, and manage workload according to risk or deadlines; Meet the needs of our business partners and internal clients; and Assist in the training of staff; and Provide specialist product knowledge; contribute to department and Company initiatives and projects.
* Skills and Behaviours Required:
* Will be required to undertake comprehensive training and development opportunities related to Operations. Prior experience in reconciliations / investment accounting preferred;
* Strong and proven investigations skills preferred (liaising with internal & external parties);
* Familiar with equities, fixed income and derivative products desired; and Proficient in basic software including MS Excel. Wider experience in Asset Management and understanding of the end-to-end asset lifecycle;
* Understanding of operational risks and control frameworks; and Prior experience of Aladdin and Tri-Optima.
* Good at analysing and solving problem with a strong handle on operational risk;
* Effective in managing your own time with ability to prioritise tasks appropriately; Open to feedback, receptive to change, challenges status quo and continually looks out for team and self- improvement opportunities;
* Excellent communicator with strong interpersonal skills; A strong team player able to develop and manage strong working relationships with global internal departments and external counterparties; and Able to adapt to changes quickly and be an advocator of an innovative culture within the team.

**Skills**
Incident Management, Investment Accounting, Fixed Income
